    concept.
  - A field present in [38;5;153mvalues[39m but not in [38;5;153mrules[39m is ignored, not an error. Forms can pass their whole value bag.
  - First failure per field wins; other fields still get validated. You get one message per bad field, not one message
    for the form.

  [1mCall site.[0m [38;5;153mapp.js[39m drops its local [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m and imports instead:

  [34mimport[39m { validate, required } [34mfrom[39m [31m"./validation.mjs"[39m;

  [34mconst[39m loginRules = { [36musername[39m: [[33mrequired[39m()], [36mpassword[39m: [[33mrequired[39m()] };
  [34mconst[39m { valid, errors } = [33mvalidate[39m({ username, password }, loginRules);

  Failure still goes to [38;5;153mconsole.error[39m — displaying errors on the page was explicitly out of scope, so I'm logging [38;5;153merrors
[39m  rather than inventing DOM markup. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m gets [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m on its script tag. [38;5;153mlogin()[39m and [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m are
  untouched.

  [1mBehavior change:[0m the login form currently rejects with one message, [38;5;153m"Missing required fields"[39m, when either field is
  blank. After this it reports per-field messages. Same accept/reject decision, different console output.

  [1mTests.[0m [38;5;153mvalidation.test.mjs[39m under [38;5;153mnode --test[39m, plus [38;5;153m"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. Covers: each
  rule maker in isolation (pass and fail); [38;5;153mvalidate[39m with all fields valid; one bad field and multiple bad fields;
  first-rule-wins ordering; unknown keys in [38;5;153mvalues[39m ignored; missing keys treated as [38;5;153mundefined[39m; empty rules object
  returns valid.

  [1mVerification.[0m [38;5;153mnpm test[39m for the module. For the page, I'd serve it locally and confirm the login form still submits on
  good input and rejects on blank — but that needs a browser, so unless you want me to drive one, I'll run the tests and
  report the page change as unverified-in-browser rather than claim it works.

